    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with a high-upside core led by **Gunnar Henderson** (78.49) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (75.59). **Gunnar Henderson** is our primary anchor against Trey Yesavage; he benefits significantly from a favorable dynamic platoon advantage (+14%) and the premium lineup spot at #2, which maximizes his exposure to potential run production. Similarly, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** capitalizes on a soft matchup against Brandon Young, with an impressive 0.371 xwOBA underpinning his status as a must-start despite the minor negative platoon adjustment. We are also aggressively deploying **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.89) and **Curtis Mead** (63.58) against Merrill Kelly; their scores are heavily inflated by the 18% SP skill advantage against Kelly, making them vital components of our mid-order construction today.\n\nOur pursuit of stolen bases remains central to our roster strategy, leading to the selection of **Nasim Nunez** (63.18) in the UTIL slot. Despite the #9 order penalty, **Nasim Nunez** earns his spot through an elite ability to exploit Kelly\u2019s slow delivery (87% SB potential), which provides a unique edge in our scarcest category. On the bench, **Josh Jung** (46.89) was the most difficult exclusion. While he maintains a strong floor, the SP skill penalty from facing Parker Messick kept him just below our threshold for starting consideration. Furthermore, while **Sam Antonacci** possesses an elite 0.379 xwOBA, his direct platoon disadvantage against Jes\u00fas Luzardo effectively neutralized his leadoff-spot bonus, ultimately pushing him out of the starting nine. \n\nRisks for the day center on the \"Lineup Pending\" status for nearly every position, which introduces significant variance into our efficiency scores. We are particularly monitoring **Liam Hicks** (43.07) and **Miguel Andujar** (40.75), both of whom are hovering near our \"below floor\" threshold. **Miguel Andujar** faces a particularly difficult hurdle, as the dynamic platoon disadvantage against Christian Scott heavily impacts his output. We advise caution with these end-of-roster pivots until the final lineups are verified, as any shift down the order could easily force these players into a bench-preservation status to protect our limited game caps for more favorable future matchups.",
